ng.** If the finding no longer reproduces on `main`, stop and write that to `FINDINGS.md` — a stale phase must never be "fixed" by inventing a change.  ## Goal  Add `.reload` (re-runs the last `:load`ed/`:run` file, erroring cleanly when there is none), `.format` (pretty-prints the current multiline buffer through `rbfmt` without executing it), and a `.format on|off` toggle that formats each entered line before execution. All three reuse the existing formatter; none changes what the formatter accepts.  ## Method  1. Read `AGENTS.md` in full. Obey every hard rule; they are not negotiable. 2. Reproduce the finding. Record the exact command and the exact wrong output. 3. Write the failing test FIRST. Watch it fail. Do not touch production code    until you have a red test that fails for the right reason. 4. Make the smallest change that turns it green. 5. Run the four gates yourself before claiming anything:     ```bash    cargo fmt --all -- --check    cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings    cargo test --all-targets    ./rbops/verify.sh phase-064    ```  6. Write `REPORT.md` in the exact shape required by `AGENTS.md` section 4.  ## Definition of done  - [ ] `.reload` after `:load` re-executes the file and reproduces its output; `.reload` with no file loaded is a clean error naming `:load`, not a panic on missing state - [ ] `.format` on an ugly-but-valid buffer prints the canonical form and leaves the buffer unexecuted (asserted: bindings unchanged after `.format`) - [ ] with the toggle on, entering `set   x    to   1` executes `set x to 1` (proved by the binding existing afterwards); with it off, the line executes verbatim - [ ] a buffer the formatter rejects is executed (or refused) exactly as with the toggle off — the toggle never converts a formatter error into a silent acceptance - [ ] edge_* tests cover `.reload` after the file was deleted since loading (clean IO error with the path), `.format` on an empty buffer (no-op, no crash), and toggle state surviving